<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan sugar output reaches 2.32 million tonnes.</title>
<headline>Pakistan sugar output reaches 2.32 million tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistan Sugar Mills Association said on Monday sugar production had reached 2.32 million tonnes by April 15 compared to 2.43 million tonnes at the same time a year ago.</p>
<p>It said mills aimed to produce 2.4 million tonnes in 1996/97, compared to 2.47 million in 1995/96 and 3.0 million in 1994/95. Dealers had bought 1.13 million tonnes, or 49 percent, of the production and 1.18 million tonnes remained at the mills.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
